# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The ground state energy obtained (-1.83 hartrees) is not too far from the correct value (-1.85 hartrees). However, the excited state energy is quite a bit off. This is similar to the erroneous behavior we saw earlier in this lesson. The energy reported for the excited state is nearly the same as that for the ground state. In the previous case, we even saw an excited state energy that was _lower_ than the reported ground state energy.\n"
msgstr "得られた基底状態エネルギー（-1.83 ハートリー）は正確な値（-1.85 ハートリー）からそれほど離れていません。しかし、励起状態エネルギーはかなりずれています。これは本レッスンで以前見た誤った挙動と同様です。励起状態として報告されたエネルギーが基底状態のそれとほぼ同じになっています。前の例では、励起状態エネルギーが報告された基底状態エネルギーよりも _低い_ という結果すら見られました。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It is not possible for a variational calculation to yield an energy that is lower than the true ground state energy. In the earlier instance, the ground state energy we obtained was not very close to the true ground state. Since we did not obtain the true ground state energy in that case, there is no contradiction. In the present case, the ground state energy was fairly close to the correct value, and yet the excited state energy seems strangely close to that same value.\n"
msgstr "変分計算で真の基底状態エネルギーより低いエネルギーが得られることはあり得ません。前の例において基底状態エネルギーが真の値に近くなかったため、矛盾は生じていませんでした。今回の場合、基底状態エネルギーは正確な値にかなり近かったにもかかわらず、励起状態エネルギーが不自然にも基底状態のエネルギーに近い値になっています。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To understand better how this happened, recall that the way we find an excited state is by requiring that the variational state be orthogonal to the ground state (using the overlap circuits and penalty terms). If we fail to obtain an accurate ground state energy (or are off by a few percent), then we also fail to obtain an accurate ground state vector! So when we require that the excited state be orthogonal to the first state we found, we were not imposing orthogonality with the true ground state, but rather with some approximation of it (sometimes a poor approximation of it). Thus, the excited state was not forced to be orthogonal to the true ground state, and our energy estimates for the excited states were actually quite close to the ground state energy.\n"
msgstr "この現象を理解するために、励起状態を求める方法を思い出してください。変分状態が基底状態と直交することを要求することで励起状態を求めています（重なり回路とペナルティ項を使用）。正確な基底状態エネルギーが得られなかった場合（数パーセントの誤差がある場合）、正確な基底状態ベクトルも得られません。そのため、励起状態を最初に求めた状態と直交させようとしても、真の基底状態との直交性を課しているのではなく、その近似値（場合によっては精度の低い近似値）との直交性を課しているにすぎません。したがって、励起状態は真の基底状態と直交するよう強制されず、結果として励起状態のエネルギー推定値が基底状態エネルギーに非常に近い値となったのです。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This will always be a concern in VQD. But in principle, this can be corrected by increasing the maximum number of iterations for the classical optimizer, imposing lower tolerance for the classical optimizer, and possibly also trying a different ansatz if we are habitually missing the true ground state. As we have seen, one may also need to modify the overlap penalties (betas). But that is really a separate issue. No penalty for overlap will keep you away from the true ground state, if you haven't found a very good estimate of the true ground state for the overlap circuit.\n"
msgstr "これは VQD において常に懸念される問題です。しかし原則として、古典的オプティマイザーの最大反復回数を増やし、許容誤差を小さく設定し、さらに真の基底状態を繰り返し外している場合には別の ansatz を試すことで改善できます。また、重なりペナルティ（betas）の調整も必要になる場合があります。しかしこれは本質的に別の問題です。重なりペナルティがどれほど適切でも、真の基底状態の良い推定値が得られていなければ、重なり回路を使って真の基底状態から離れた状態を維持することはできません。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Optimization: max-cut {#optimization-max-cut}"
msgstr "最適化：Max-Cut {#optimization-max-cut}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The maximum cut (max-cut) problem is a combinatorial optimization problem that involves dividing the vertices of a graph into two disjoint sets such that the number of edges between the two sets is maximized. More formally, given an undirected graph $G=(V,E)$, where $V$ is the set of vertices and $E$ is the set of edges, the max-cut problem asks to partition the vertices into two disjoint subsets, $S$ and $T$, such that the number of edges with one endpoint in $S$ and the other in $T$ is maximized.\n"
msgstr "最大カット（Max-Cut）問題は、グラフの頂点を二つの互いに素な集合に分割し、二つの集合間のエッジ数を最大化する組み合わせ最適化問題です。より形式的に述べると、無向グラフ $G=(V,E)$（$V$ は頂点の集合、$E$ はエッジの集合）が与えられたとき、一方の端点が $S$ に、もう一方の端点が $T$ にあるエッジの数が最大になるように、頂点を二つの互いに素な部分集合 $S$ と $T$ に分割する問題です。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can apply max-cut to solve a various problems, such as clustering, network design, and phase transitions. We'll start by creating a problem graph:\n"
msgstr "Max-Cut はクラスタリング、ネットワーク設計、相転移といった様々な問題に応用できます。まず問題グラフを作成します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/3eb71b79-a988-4807-aa88-7fb25a78a236-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![前のコードセルの出力](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/3eb71b79-a988-4807-aa88-7fb25a78a236-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This problem can be expressed as a binary optimization problem. For each node $0 \\leq i < n$, where $n$ is the number of nodes of the graph (in this case $n=4$), we will consider the binary variable $x_i$. This variable will have the value $1$ if node $i$ is one of the groups that we'll label $1$ and $0$ if it's in the other group, that we'll label as $0$. We will also denote as $w_{ij}$ (element $(i,j)$ of the adjacency matrix $w$) the weight of the edge that goes from node $i$ to node $j$. Because the graph is undirected, $w_{ij}=w_{ji}$. Then we can formulate our problem as maximizing the following cost function:\n"
msgstr "この問題は二値最適化問題として表現できます。グラフのノード数を $n$（今回は $n=4$）とし、$0 \\leq i < n$ の各ノード $i$ に対して二値変数 $x_i$ を導入します。この変数は、ノード $i$ が「グループ 1」に属する場合は $1$、「グループ 0」に属する場合は $0$ をとります。また、隣接行列 $w$ の要素 $(i,j)$ を $w_{ij}$ とし、ノード $i$ からノード $j$ へのエッジの重みを表します。グラフは無向なので $w_{ij}=w_{ji}$ が成り立ちます。この設定のもと、次のコスト関数を最大化する問題として定式化できます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{x})\n"
"& =\\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i(1-x_j)\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{x})\n"
"& =\\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i(1-x_j)\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_ix_j\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_ix_j\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i 2w_{ij} x_ix_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i 2w_{ij} x_ix_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To solve this problem with a quantum computer, we are going to express the cost function as the expected value of an observable. However, the observables that Qiskit admits natively consist of Pauli operators, that have eigenvalues $1$ and $-1$ instead of $0$ and $1$. That's why we are going to make the following change of variable:\n"
msgstr "この問題を量子コンピュータで解くために、コスト関数をオブザーバブルの期待値として表現します。ただし、Qiskit がネイティブに扱うオブザーバブルはパウリ演算子で構成されており、固有値は $0$ と $1$ ではなく $1$ と $-1$ をとります。そのため、次の変数変換を行います。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Where $\\vec{x}=(x_0,x_1,\\cdots ,x_{n-1})$. We can use the adjacency matrix $w$ to comfortably access the weights of all the edge. This will be used to obtain our cost function:\n"
msgstr "ここで $\\vec{x}=(x_0,x_1,\\cdots ,x_{n-1})$ とします。隣接行列 $w$ を使うと全エッジの重みに簡単にアクセスでき、コスト関数の導出に役立ちます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"z_i = 1-2x_i \\rightarrow x_i = \\frac{1-z_i}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"z_i = 1-2x_i \\rightarrow x_i = \\frac{1-z_i}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This implies that:\n"
msgstr "これにより次のことが導かれます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{lcl} x_i=0 & \\rightarrow & z_i=1 \\\\ x_i=1 & \\rightarrow & z_i=-1.\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{lcl} x_i=0 & \\rightarrow & z_i=1 \\\\ x_i=1 & \\rightarrow & z_i=-1.\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "So the new cost function we want to maximize is:\n"
msgstr "したがって、最大化すべき新しいコスト関数は次のようになります。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{z})\n"
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} \\bigg(\\frac{1-z_i}{2}\\bigg)\\bigg(1-\\frac{1-z_j}{2}\\bigg)\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{z})\n"
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} \\bigg(\\frac{1-z_i}{2}\\bigg)\\bigg(1-\\frac{1-z_j}{2}\\bigg)\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} z_iz_j\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} z_iz_j\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Moreover, the natural tendency of a quantum computer is to find minima (usually the lowest energy) instead of maxima so instead of maximizing $C(\\vec{z})$ we are going to minimize:\n"
msgstr "また、量子コンピュータは最大値ではなく最小値（通常は最低エネルギー）を見つけようとするため、$C(\\vec{z})$ を最大化するのではなく、次の式を最小化します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"-C(\\vec{z}) =  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"-C(\\vec{z}) =  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have a cost function to minimize whose variables can have the values $-1$ and $1$, we can make the following analogy with the Pauli $Z$:\n"
msgstr "変数が $-1$ と $1$ の値をとるコスト関数を最小化する問題が得られたので、パウリ $Z$ との対応付けを次のように行います。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"z_i \\equiv Z_i = \\overbrace{I}^{n-1}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{Z}^{i} \\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{I}^{0}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"z_i \\equiv Z_i = \\overbrace{I}^{n-1}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{Z}^{i} \\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{I}^{0}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In other words, the variable $z_i$ will be equivalent to a $Z$ gate acting on qubit $i$. Moreover:\n"
msgstr "つまり、変数 $z_i$ は qubit $i$ に作用する $Z$ Gate に対応します。さらに：\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle \\rightarrow \\langle x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 |Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle \\rightarrow \\langle x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 |Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Then the observable we are going to consider is:\n"
msgstr "したがって、考えるべきオブザーバブルは次のようになります。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} Z_iZ_j\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} Z_iZ_j\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "to which we will have to add the independent term afterwards:\n"
msgstr "これに後から独立項を加える必要があります。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\texttt{offset} = - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"The operator is a linear combination of terms with Z operators on nodes connected by an edge (recall that the 0th qubit is farthest right): $IIZZ + IZIZ + IZZI + ZIIZ + ZZII$. Once the operator is constructed, the ansatz for the QAOA algorithm can easily be built by using the `QAOAAnsatz` circuit from the Qiskit circuit library.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\texttt{offset} = - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/d28c4262-a080-4fe4-9427-762326184cd8-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "この演算子は、エッジで結ばれたノード上の Z 演算子を含む項の線形結合です（0 番目の qubit が最も右側にあることに注意）：$IIZZ + IZIZ + IZZI + ZIIZ + ZZII$。演算子が構成できれば、QAOA アルゴリズムの ansatz は Qiskit Circuit ライブラリの `QAOAAnsatz` Circuit を使って簡単に構築できます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We now set an initial set of random parameters:\n"
msgstr "![前のコードセルの出力](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/d28c4262-a080-4fe4-9427-762326184cd8-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Any classical optimizer can be used to minimize the cost function. On a real quantum system, an optimizer designed for non-smooth cost function landscapes usually does better. Here we use the [COBYLA routine](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/optimize.minimize-cobyla.html#optimize-minimize-cobyla) from SciPy via the minimize function.\n"
msgstr "初期パラメーターをランダムに設定します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because we are iteratively executing many calls to Runtime, we make use of a session to execute all calls within a single block. Moreover, for QAOA, the solution is encoded in the output distribution of the ansatz circuit bound with the optimal parameters from the minimization. Therefore, we will need a Sampler primitive, and will instantiate it with the same session\n"
"And run our minimization routine:\n"
msgstr "コスト関数の最小化には任意の古典的オプティマイザーを使用できます。実際の量子システムでは、滑らかでないコスト関数の景観に対応したオプティマイザーが通常より良い結果を出します。ここでは SciPy の minimize 関数を介して [COBYLA ルーチン](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/optimize.minimize-cobyla.html#optimize-minimize-cobyla) を使用します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The solution vector of parameter angles (`x`), when plugged into the ansatz circuit, yields the graph partitioning that we were looking for.\n"
msgstr "Runtime への呼び出しを繰り返し実行するため、セッションを利用してすべての呼び出しを一つのブロック内で実行します。また、QAOA の解は最小化で得られた最適パラメーターを ansatz Circuit に割り当てたときの出力分布に符号化されています。そのため Sampler プリミティブが必要であり、同じセッションでインスタンス化します。最小化ルーティンを実行します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/686ee28e-9327-40d1-8d7c-3ec527160f01-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "パラメーター角度のベクトル（`x`）を ansatz Circuit に代入すると、求めていたグラフの分割結果が得られます。\n"

